---
source: compiler-core/src/javascript/tests/module_lets.rs
expression: "\npub let b = a + 1\n\npub let a = 1\n"
---
----- SOURCE CODE

pub let b = a + 1

pub let a = 1


----- ERROR
error: Value used before it is defined
  ┌─ /src/one/two.gleam:2:1
  │
2 │ pub let b = a + 1
  │ ^^^^^^^^^ This reads `a`
3 │ 
4 │ pub let a = 1
  │ --------- Defined here

`a` is bound below this one, and a binding at module level
runs when the module is loaded, in the order it was written. So
`a` has no value yet when this one runs.
